[I] Archive OpenPGP keys on paper

[T] Paperkey extracts only the secret parts of an OpenPGP secret key, so it
[T] can be printed on paper for long term backup. The key can later be
[T] restored by combining the printed data with the public key.

[U] https://www.jabberwocky.com/software/paperkey/

[A] Paperkey Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

